## F. Documentation maintenance protocol

Where knowledge goes:

| Kind of knowledge | Home |
|---|---|
| Universal behaviour + routing | `.github/copilot-instructions.md` (keep < ~200 lines; `AGENTS.md` if shared with other AI tools) |
| Current project truth / what's live where | `docs/ai-context/PROJECT.md` |
| Decisions, failures, corrections (durable, dated) | this file |
| Hard rules scoped to file paths | `.github/instructions/*.instructions.md` (`applyTo:` frontmatter) |
| Per-area orientation (50–150 lines) | `docs/ai-context/<area>.md` |
| Canonical deep reference | `docs/<UPPERCASE>.md` |
| Deferred work | `docs/<AREA>_BACKLOG.md` |
| Multi-step procedures | `.github/skills/*/SKILL.md` |
| Machine-private session pointers | any IDE- or CLI-local memory the tool keeps (NOT visible to teammates or other agents — anything durable must also land above) |

Rules of the protocol:
1. **One home per fact.** Everywhere else links to it.
2. **Date-stamp state claims.** "Live on prod 2026-07-10" ages gracefully; "live on prod" becomes a lie.
3. **Prune on contact.** A verified-stale entry is fixed or deleted in the same turn. Conflicts you
   can't resolve get a ⚠ CONFLICT flag for the owner, never a silent pick.
4. **New durable lesson → the right home, same turn.** Path-scoped gotcha → instruction file;
   decision/failure → this file; state change → `PROJECT.md` + changelog.
5. **Don't persist:** session-specific context, one-off values, anything derivable from code/git in
   seconds, generic engineering advice.

